{
  "id": "dalton_s_law",
  "title": "Dalton's Law",
  "description": "Calculate total pressure and partial pressures of gas mixtures using Dalton's Law of Partial Pressures. The total pressure of a gas mixture equals the sum of the partial pressures of individual gases.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Dalton's Law of Partial Pressures\n\nThe total pressure exerted by a mixture of gases is the sum of the partial pressures of the individual gases:\n\n**ptotal = p1 + p2 + ... + pn = Σ pi**\n\nFor an ideal gas, the partial pressure is calculated using:\n\n**pi = (n × R × T) / V**\n\nWhere:\n- **ptotal** = total pressure (Pa, psi)\n- **pi** = partial pressure of individual gas (Pa, psi)\n- **n** = number of moles of the gas\n- **R** = universal gas constant (8.3145 J/(mol·K))\n- **T** = absolute temperature (K)\n- **V** = volume (m³)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "n_moles",
          "label": "Number of Moles",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "mol"
        },
        {
          "id": "temperature",
          "label": "Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 300,
          "unit": "K"
        },
        {
          "id": "volume",
          "label": "Volume",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.005,
          "unit": "m³"
        },
        {
          "id": "gas_constant",
          "label": "Universal Gas Constant",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 8.3145,
          "unit": "J/(mol·K)"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "partial_pressure_pa",
          "label": "Partial Pressure",
          "formula": "(inputs.n_moles * inputs.gas_constant * inputs.temperature) / inputs.volume",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "partial_pressure_kpa",
          "label": "Partial Pressure",
          "formula": "((inputs.n_moles * inputs.gas_constant * inputs.temperature) / inputs.volume) / 1000",
          "unit": "kPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "partial_pressure_psi",
          "label": "Partial Pressure",
          "formula": "((inputs.n_moles * inputs.gas_constant * inputs.temperature) / inputs.volume) * 0.000145038",
          "unit": "psi",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Gas Component",
        "Number of Moles",
        "Partial Pressure (Pa)",
        "Partial Pressure (kPa)",
        "Partial Pressure (psi)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
